  "notes": "The commercial hinge between Southern club rap and Top-40, and the research says where that shows: *\"the highest melodic content in this section apart from Dungeon Family\"*, over 4–8 bar melodic phrases with real changes rather than crunk's static i. So this file's centre of gravity is the melody block — `phraseBars` reaches 8, `densityPerBar` [5, 10], `structure` `question_answer`, an arch-weighted contour — and the chord block carries genuine two- and four-chord families in both the major (I–IV, I–V–vi–IV) and minor (i–VII–VI) forms. `session.halfTime` is **false**, the backbeat is on 2 and 4, and the 16th hats are programmed with swing, which is the authored `session.swing.amount` of 0.56. ⛔ **The bass follows the chord loop, not the kick**, so it is a real part rather than the 808: `drums.bass808.role` is `counter_riff` — the engine's only way to stop the 808 claiming the bassline — and the `bassline` block is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.70. ⚠ That role also lets the 808 keep a pitch it slid to, which is not a Jermaine Dupri behaviour; `slideProb` stays low so it is rare. ⚠ The research's \"short-to-medium decay so the melody reads\" has no engine stage — the 808's envelope is not authored anywhere — and is recorded only here. ⚠ `confidence` is medium: the research rates era and credits medium-high but the **parameters medium**, and marks the numbers [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ Two bands are documented: 88–104 straight for the main body of work, and 70–80 half-time for the snap-era singles. This model is the first; the half-time snap form is the parent genre's `snap` mode and is reachable there. ⚠ Fill fingerprint for this batch: `gapProb` 0.30 / `descendProb` 0.60 / `rampJitter` 14. ⛔ `session.scales` **widens** its parent's set rather than narrowing it: `major` and `dorian` are not among crunk's four, and the convention elsewhere is that an artist narrows its genre's scales and never reaches outside them. They are here because the research's keys row says \"major and dorian\" and the I–IV and I–V–vi–IV families point at the wrong degrees without them. This model wants a pop-rap archetype to extend rather than crunk.",
